  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q2_Connectivity
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: The server is 192.168.1.10 and the client is 192.168.1.20, both with
    subnet mask 255.255.255.0. Are they on the same network?
  choices:
  - "Yes \u2014 the mask makes 192.168.1 the network part, and both share it"
  - "No \u2014 the last octet differs, so they are different networks"
  - Only if a default gateway is configured on both
  - Only if they are plugged into the same switch port
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  points: 10
  explanation: 255.255.255.0 (a /24) means the first three octets identify the network
    and the last identifies the host. .10 and .20 are two hosts on one network, so
    they reach each other without a router.
